# make_qtext_chunks.py - quest conditional texts (pasted from the Data Table tool) -> qtexts_en.json and qtexts_chunks_en/names_0000.json
import os; os.chdir(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "..", "work"))   # scripts always run with work/ as the working directory
import json, os

TEXTS = {
92456: """If I have to teach you herbalism you can at least make yourself useful. I have an errand I need run. For a city of mages, Dalaran has a surprising interest in botany. The Kirin Tor keep to themselves, but I would love a sample of their mana-infused vegetation. You're clearly someone who is comfortable being where people don't want you, maybe you could find a way into the city. If you do, bring me back whatever is growing in their central garden.""",
92595: """<Illaya smiles warmly at you.> I am glad you returned to speak with me, child of the winds. I knew it the first moment you walked into my presence, that you were strong in the skysight. Even for a Shaman, you show particular aptitude in our gift. Come, let us speak about the mandate of the Windshapers, the nature of our struggles on Zephras, and the plight of our people.""",
92596: """The aura of arcane energy that surrounds you is strong, even for a mage such as yourself. Come, let us sit and speak some on the nature of the arcane and the plight of our homeland.""",
95250: """Ah, a fellow human. It's about time Lordaeron sent reinforcements. My master has already charged into the fray and has ordered me to maintain my post. It has been quite some time, however. I don't dare trust this task to any of these filthy half breeds, but if I could impose on you a favor, I beg of you to find me the Grand Marshal. He is the tallest, most statuesque hero you've ever laid eyes on. You'll know him when you see him.""",
96391: """<The map you are holding seems to show a complex series of underground tunnels and highways that all seem to converge on a point underneath Ironforge itself. You can't be sure what the runes say as they are written in the ugly jagged rune language of the Dark Iron dwarves, but you can guess at the purpose of these tunnels. As you are reading the map, a gust of wind washes over you and you can faintly hear a dwarven voice carried on it, urging you to seek out an Earthseer named "Farsen".>""",
97485: """Blessings of An'she, child. We have a tradition of scattering incense to the winds, and I was wondering if you'd be interested in honoring our tradition. You will need to craft the incense by purchasing herbs from Nida, cedar from Nata, sinew thread from Mahu in the mid rise, and ceremonial flint and tinder from Naal on the upper rise. Once you have these items, combine them and spread them off the south facing cliff of Hunter's Rise. You will find a mat and incense at the ceremonial site.""",
97979: """You are born kaldorei--the children of the stars--and shall become a great priestess of our goddess Elune. Her grace may illuminate our strengths, helping our strikes hit true, or it may help conceal us just as the moon may eclipse the sun. Our Long Vigil after the defense of Mount Hyjal has ended, and we have joined an Alliance of others--which you will meet in due time. For now, you are nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil. Demonstrate Mother Moon's gifts, and bask in her blessings.""",
98027: """<The silver necklace in your hands gleams gently as you examine it. The small crescent moon shape is evocative of Mother Moon herself. Upon flipping the necklace over there is a small inscription: "We love you, Maliynn". Perhaps it belongs to Maliynn in Astranaar?>""",
98251: """Gaaah! I'm so angry. They said Ashenvale was easy to follow. Easy for who? The beasts? The birds? One moment I was gathering an herb, the next I'm trapped in this ravine. Do I truly have to circle half the forest to reach where I stood just moments ago? When I'm like this, my spells grow volatile and behave... differently. Could you thin the wildlife nearby? Their stupid digging grates on me. I despise this cursed forest.""",
98299: """If there is one thing we do know, it is that Arugal is responsible for worgen within Silverpine. Be it his own machinations or otherwise. What we don't know is how it spreads. While I research a way to stop the curse, our first priority is to contain it. It appears this affliction cannot infect forsaken such as ourselves, but a large group of humans have gathered by the Greymane Wall. Go to the wall and put down these refugees before they have a chance to become servants for Arugal.""",
98321: """Hoha! Good to see a fellow blacksmith who's not afraid to get their hands dirty. If yer lookin' fer work, I'm afraid I'm a little short on supplies at the moment. Our most reliable source of ore has been overrun by wendigo and now the cave has been abandoned. The miners had to drop everything when they fled! Say, why don't ye poke yer head around the Grizzled Den to the west and see if you can find some of our missing shipments. It would save us a great deal o' trouble.""",
98389: """If you remember but one thing, know this: not even death can stop the Light. This we have in common with all Forsaken--we have overcome what the living view as their end. However, some even among our own fear us; they suspect we will smite them as some monstrosity. In truth, our relationship with undeath is complex, but we are not here to hurt our own. Help me show the others this. Venture to Night's Web Hollow to the northwest and free the freshly raised fools trapped by the spiders there. Then they will see our nature.""",
99144: """Light bless you for finding me. I was on my way from Bandarion Keep to deliver a message to Shari Stilwell in Brill when these monsters captured me. They wield the Light with a hatred in their hearts that makes what's left of my blood seethe. It goes against all we stand for! <Bareth Dawnstone steadies himself.> Our ranks are thin. If you would aid me in escaping this place, I would be forever grateful.""",
}

rows = [{"quest_id": k, "text": v} for k, v in TEXTS.items()]
json.dump(rows, open("qtexts_en.json", "w", encoding="utf-8"), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)

texts = sorted({r["text"] for r in rows})
os.makedirs("qtexts_chunks_en", exist_ok=True)
with open("qtexts_chunks_en/names_0000.json", "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
    json.dump([{"i": i, "en": t} for i, t in enumerate(texts)], f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
print(len(rows), "quest texts;", len(texts), "unique; 1 chunk")
